{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.DescentLemma","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.DescentLemma","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Hom","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_descentSurjective_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_descentSurjective_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-lemma.lean#L103-L115","doc":"**The claim is refutable at a concrete algebra map**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nThe diagonal `ℤ →ₐ[ℤ] ℤ × ℤ` is an algebra homomorphism whose image misses\n`(1, 0)`: a preimage would have to equal `1` in the first coordinate and `0`\nin the second. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descentSurjective_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descentSurjective_comp","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-lemma.lean#L86-L101","doc":"**Descent through the tower, derived.**\n\nIf each one-step descent is surjective then so is their composite, so\nsurjectivity propagates from level `n` down to any lower level of the brane\ntower `{Aₙ}_{n ≥ 0}`.\n\nThis is why the lemma is stated for a tower rather than a single pair, and it\nis the one consequence obtainable without constructing `End_C(Aₙ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descent_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descent_surjective","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-lemma.lean#L73-L84","doc":"**Surjectivity of a descent homomorphism** ([`lem:descent`]), as a\nproposition over a caller-supplied algebra map.\n\n`𝔡ₙ : End_C(Aₙ) →ₐ[R] End_C(A_{n-1})` is surjective.\n\n**Named, not asserted.** An algebra homomorphism rather than a linear one,\nmatching the `.md`; see the module docstring for the two claims of the lemma\nthat remain unencoded. ","signatureChunk":0}]}